menu "Pilot Kit Box"

    config PK_BLE_ENABLED
        bool "Initialise BLE GATT server at boot (requires C6 esp_hosted slave firmware)"
        default n
        help
            When enabled, app_main() calls ble_gatt_init() which in turn
            kicks NimBLE on top of the ESP-Hosted VHCI transport. NimBLE
            assumes the BT controller (living on the on-board ESP32-C6)
            is responsive — if the C6 hasn't been flashed with the
            esp_hosted slave firmware yet, the call eventually trips an
            ESP_ERROR_CHECK() inside the hosted vhci_drv.c and aborts
            the whole P4 firmware. The hosted layer offers no graceful
            failure path for that case.

            Default is OFF so a freshly-cloned firmware boots cleanly
            on a board whose C6 still ships the factory AT firmware.
            Once you flash the C6 slave (see docs/hardware/c6_slave_firmware.md)
            flip this on with `idf.py menuconfig` and rebuild.

endmenu
